---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getStats } from '../lib/stats';

const { fromRepo, fromServices, builtAt } = getStats ? await getStats() : { fromRepo: [], fromServices: [], builtAt: new Date() };
const built = builtAt.toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace('T', ' ') + ' UTC';
---

<Base
  title="Stats — Agentic Field Notes"
  description="How many notes, how many words, how many readers. Including the numbers that are zero."
>
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top: 56px;">
    <h1
      style="margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 620px; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 40px); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.028em;"
    >
      Stats
    </h1>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 8px; max-width: 620px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-2);">
      This page exists because of <a href="/notes/02-nobody-was-using-it">No. 02</a>. The product
      that used to be at this domain had a dashboard that listed the most recent signups — which
      looks identical whether you have six users or six hundred. It was structurally incapable of
      reporting failure.
    </p>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 40px; max-width: 620px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-2);">
      So the numbers here are counts, not feeds, and a number that is zero says zero. A number that
      cannot be read says so rather than being estimated.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mono-label" style="padding-bottom: 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);">
      From the repository &nbsp;·&nbsp; exact
    </h2>
    {
      fromRepo.map((s) => (
        <div
          style="display: flex; gap: 24px; align-items: baseline; padding: 24px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); flex-wrap: wrap;"
        >
          <p
            style="margin: 0; min-width: 140px; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 34px; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;"
          >
            {s.value}
          </p>
          <div style="flex: 1 1 280px; min-width: 0;">
            <p style="margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;">{s.label}</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted);">{s.note}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))
    }

    <h2
      class="mono-label"
      style="margin-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);"
    >
      From outside services &nbsp;·&nbsp; at build time
    </h2>
    {
      fromServices.map((s) => (
        <div
          style="display: flex; gap: 24px; align-items: baseline; padding: 24px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); flex-wrap: wrap;"
        >
          <p
            style={`margin: 0; min-width: 140px; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; ${s.pending ? 'font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted);' : 'font-size: 34px;'}`}
          >
            {s.value}
          </p>
          <div style="flex: 1 1 280px; min-width: 0;">
            <p style="margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;">{s.label}</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted);">{s.note}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))
    }

    <p style="margin: 32px 0 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted);">
      Built {built}. The site is static, so these are correct as of the last deploy, not live.
    </p>

    <p style="margin: 24px 0 0; max-width: 620px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--muted);">
      Readers are counted with Google Analytics, configured without ad signals or personalisation
      and with IP anonymisation on. It is here to count, not to profile. Nothing on this site reads
      or stores anything else about you, and there is no account to have.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
